        <h1>About me</h1>
        <p>I take technical platforms from pilot to production and make sure the people who depend on them actually succeed with them. My work sits where infrastructure, customers and funding meet: scoping what a partner needs, getting it deployed, and showing the results to the people who pay for it.</p>
        <p>Most recently I was the Senior Technical Project Manager for <a href="{{ '/work/chameleon-platform/' | url }}">Chameleon Cloud</a> at the University of Chicago, an NSF-funded cloud platform with 15,000+ users. I kept $14M in grants renewed, cut onboarding time by about 40%, and led <a href="{{ '/work/chameleon-ai-docs/' | url }}">an AI documentation pilot</a> using retrieval-augmented generation that brought in $2.5M in new funding. Before that I ran the national rollout of <a href="{{ '/work/floto-rollout/' | url }}">FLOTO</a>, taking a broadband measurement platform from zero to more than 1,000 edge devices for over a dozen State Broadband Offices.</p>
        <p>I started my career at <a href="{{ '/work/criterion-economics/' | url }}">Criterion Economics</a>, doing economic analysis for Fortune 500 clients in major litigation, and then earned an MS in Computational Analysis and Public Policy at UChicago.</p>
        <p>Since leaving Chameleon I've been running <a href="{{ '/work/llm-ticket-triage/' | url }}">hands-on LLM deployment experiments</a> on Fireworks AI and the Anthropic API: comparing open and frontier models on cost, latency and accuracy, fine-tuning small models, and writing up what I'd tell a customer. I'm looking for roles in AI deployment, technical program management and solutions work on AI and cloud infrastructure.</p>
        <p>I'm based in Chicago and speak English and Spanish.</p>
